---
layout: data-page.njk
title: "Recording now"
description: "What Elixir MCP is recording at this moment: the last battle seen, battles this hour, and how many collectors are running."
permalink: /data/now/index.html
canonical: /data/now
dataNav: now
---
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
{%- set n = "—" %}
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">Recording now</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="margin: 0; max-width: 60ch">
    The only live numbers on this half of the site.
  </p>
</div>

{#- With JavaScript off this shows the deploy-time values and still reads
    true, which is why the numbers are rendered server-side and replaced
    only if the fetch succeeds. -#}
<section class="panel" style="border-color: var(--ok-edge); max-width: 520px">
  <div class="panel__body">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 11px">
      <span class="chip chip--ok"><span class="chip__dot"></span>recording</span>
      <span style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600">Right now</span>
      <span class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-faint)">live · cached 60s</span>
    </div>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 22px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-body)">
      <span>last battle <strong data-live="last" style="color: var(--ink)">{% if t %}{{ t.newest_battle | day }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</strong></span>
      <span><strong data-live="hour" style="color: var(--ink)">{{ n }}</strong> this hour</span>
      <span><strong data-live="collectors" style="color: var(--ink)">{% if t %}{{ t.collectors_active }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</strong> collectors</span>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote" style="margin: 11px 0 0">
      Operators get the whole picture in the <a href="/status/service">console&rsquo;s status page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script defer src="/assets/data-live.js"></script>
